{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int MOD=1000000007;\ninline int addmod(int a,int b){ if((a+=b)>=MOD) a-=MOD; return a; }\ninline int mulmod(int a,int b){ long long t=1LL*a*b; if(t>=MOD) t%=MOD; return (int)t; }\n\nstruct Matr {\n    int m[35][35];\n    void clear(){ memset(m,0,sizeof(m)); }\n    void identity(){ clear(); for(int i=0;i<35;i++) m[i][i]=1; }\n    const int* operator[](int i) const{ return m[i]; }\n    int* operator[](int i){ return m[i]; }\n};\n\nMatr addMat(const Matr& a, const Matr& b){\n    Matr c; c.clear();\n    for(int i=0;i<35;i++) for(int j=0;j<35;j++) c[i][j]=addmod(a[i][j],b[i][j]);\n    return c;\n}\nMatr mulScalar(const Matr& a, int x){\n    Matr c=a;\n    for(int i=0;i<35;i++) for(int j=0;j<35;j++) c[i][j]=mulmod(c[i][j],x);\n    return c;\n}\nMatr mulMat(const Matr& a, const Matr& b){\n    Matr c; c.clear();\n    for(int i=0;i<35;i++){\n        for(int k=0;k<35;k++){\n            int aik=a[i][k];\n            if(aik){\n                for(int j=0;j<35;j++) c[i][j]=addmod(c[i][j],mulmod(aik,b[k][j]));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return c;\n}\n\ntypedef long long ll;\nll n;\nint K;\nvector<int> digit;\nMatr A[65][35], S[65][35], P[65][35], ans;\n\nint main(){\n    scanf(\"%lld%d\",&n,&K);\n    for(int i=0;i<K;i++){\n        A[0][i].identity();\n        for(int j=0;j<=K;j++) A[0][i][i][j]=1;\n    }\n    ll len=K;\n    for(int i=1; len<=n; i++, len*=K){\n        S[i-1][K-1]=A[i-1][K-1];\n        for(int j=K-2;j>=0;j--) S[i-1][j]=mulMat(A[i-1][j],S[i-1][j+1]);\n        P[i-1][0]=A[i-1][0];\n        for(int j=1;j<K;j++) P[i-1][j]=mulMat(P[i-1][j-1],A[i-1][j]);\n        A[i][0]=S[i-1][0];\n        for(int j=1;j<K;j++) A[i][j]=mulMat(S[i-1][j],P[i-1][j-1]);\n    }\n    while(n){\n        digit.push_back(n%K);\n        n/=K;\n    }\n    int s=0;\n    ans.identity();\n    for(int i=digit.size()-1;i>=0;i--){\n        for(int j=0;j<digit[i];j++)\n            ans=mulMat(ans,A[i][(j+s)%K]);\n        s=(s+digit[i])%K;\n    }\n    int res=1;\n    for(int i=0;i<K;i++) res=addmod(res,ans[i][K]);\n    printf(\"%d\\n\",res);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef addmod(a, b):\n    a += b\n    if a >= MOD:\n        a -= MOD\n    return a\n\ndef mulmod(a, b):\n    return (a * b) % MOD\n\ndef mat_add(a, b):\n    n = len(a)\n    c = [[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            c[i][j] = addmod(a[i][j], b[i][j])\n    return c\n\ndef mat_mul_scalar(a, x):\n    n = len(a)\n    c = [row[:] for row in a]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            c[i][j] = mulmod(c[i][j], x)\n    return c\n\ndef mat_mul(a, b):\n    n = len(a)\n    c = [[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for k in range(n):\n            aik = a[i][k]\n            if aik:\n                for j in range(n):\n                    c[i][j] = addmod(c[i][j], mulmod(aik, b[k][j]))\n    return c\n\ndef mat_identity(n):\n    c = [[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        c[i][i] = 1\n    return c\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    K = int(data[1])\n    N = K + 1  # matrix size\n\n    # A[i][j] for i=0..max_power, j=0..K-1\n    A = []\n    # first level\n    A0 = []\n    for d in range(K):\n        mat = mat_identity(N)\n        mat[d][K] = 1\n        A0.append(mat)\n    A.append(A0)\n\n    length = K\n    i = 1\n    while length <= n:\n        # compute S[i-1] and P[i-1]\n        S_prev = [None]*K\n        P_prev = [None]*K\n        # S from right to left\n        S_prev[K-1] = A[i-1][K-1]\n        for j in range(K-2, -1, -1):\n            S_prev[j] = mat_mul(A[i-1][j], S_prev[j+1])\n        # P from left to right\n        P_prev[0] = A[i-1][0]\n        for j in range(1, K):\n            P_prev[j] = mat_mul(P_prev[j-1], A[i-1][j])\n        # compute A[i]\n        Ai = [None]*K\n        Ai[0] = S_prev[0]\n        for j in range(1, K):\n            Ai[j] = mat_mul(S_prev[j], P_prev[j-1])\n        A.append(Ai)\n        length *= K\n        i += 1\n\n    # digits of n in base K\n    digits = []\n    temp = n\n    while temp:\n        digits.append(temp % K)\n        temp //= K\n    if not digits:\n        digits = [0]\n\n    ans = mat_identity(N)\n    s = 0\n    for idx in range(len(digits)-1, -1, -1):\n        d = digits[idx]\n        for j in range(d):\n            ans = mat_mul(ans, A[idx][(j + s) % K])\n        s = (s + d) % K\n\n    res = 1\n    for i in range(K):\n        res = addmod(res, ans[i][K])\n    print(res)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.364403477869928e-06, -0.023251153528690338, -2.169585604860913e-05, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00013362467871047556, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -7.533743337262422e-05